From bc96f2493278df3c08764a09b16641212bfb9932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:54:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 129/638] [AROS] Trace the exposed DevTools bridge

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-phase-3
AI_STATUS: diagnostic
ROOT_CAUSE: Run 0131 loads the command harness and posts Runtime.evaluate, but even about:blank plus --timeout=10000 remains pending. The harness installs its timeout only after Target.createTarget and Target.attachToTarget, so the unresolved boundary is the exposed page-to-browser DevTools bridge before navigation.
FIX_REASON: Log AROS BrowserToPageConnector initialization, page Runtime.bindingCalled payloads, browser protocol responses, and page Runtime.evaluate delivery through Chromium logging/debug.resource. This distinguishes a request that never crosses into the browser from a response that cannot re-enter the renderer.
SCOPE: content/browser/devtools/protocol/target_handler.cc
VALIDATION: AROS content/browser target_handler.o cross-compiled; artifact 33 records a stable pending Runtime.evaluate with the file URL removed.
RISK: AROS-only INFO diagnostics can expose DevTools command payloads in debug logs during bring-up; no protocol behavior changes.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: staged harness pack -> executeCommands runs -> about:blank still pending -> trace exposed CDP request/response crossings
---
 .../devtools/protocol/target_handler.cc        | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/target_handler.cc b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/target_handler.cc
